---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Solo Ghost"
  description="How Solo Ghost handles information submitted through its website and SG-RVA01 evaluation services."
>
  <div class="container privacy-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">SOLO GHOST / PRIVACY</p>

    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p class="updated">Last updated: November 1, 2026</p>

    <p class="intro">
      Solo Ghost respects the privacy of individuals who visit our
      website, request product evaluations, or access our engineering
      evaluation services.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>

      <p>
        When you request an SG-RVA01 evaluation, we collect your name,
        organization, email address, and description of your intended
        evaluation purpose.
      </p>

      <p>
        When you access an approved evaluation, we also maintain
        information needed to administer invitations, activation,
        session authentication, evaluation expiry, and access revocation.
      </p>

      <p>
        Our infrastructure and security services may process technical
        information such as IP addresses, request timestamps, browser
        information, and authentication-related identifiers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. How we use information</h2>

      <p>We use this information to:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Review evaluation requests.</li>
        <li>Communicate with applicants.</li>
        <li>Issue and administer approved evaluation access.</li>
        <li>Maintain service security and investigate misuse.</li>
        <li>Diagnose technical problems and maintain service reliability.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Submitting an evaluation request does not guarantee approval
        or access.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Service providers</h2>

      <p>
        Solo Ghost uses third-party infrastructure and communication
        services to operate its website and evaluation platform.
        These include Cloudflare for website infrastructure and
        security, Resend for email delivery, and cloud hosting
        infrastructure for the evaluation application.
      </p>

      <p>
        Information may be processed by these providers as required
        to deliver their services. Processing and storage locations
        may depend on the provider and service configuration.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Evaluation access and security</h2>

      <p>
        SG-RVA01 evaluation access is invitation-based. Approved
        evaluations use authentication and time-limited access.
        Access may expire or be revoked.
      </p>

      <p>
        We use technical safeguards intended to protect evaluation
        records and restrict unauthorized access. No internet-based
        service can guarantee absolute security.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Cookies and authentication</h2>

      <p>
        Our evaluation service uses authentication-related cookies
        to maintain authorized customer sessions.
      </p>

      <p>
        Additional technical information may be processed by
        infrastructure and security services, including automated
        abuse-prevention mechanisms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Information retention</h2>

      <p>
        Evaluation-request information and related access records
        are retained as needed for evaluation administration,
        security, operational review, and applicable legal obligations.
      </p>

      <p>
        We review retention requirements as our services develop.
        Information that is no longer required will be considered
        for deletion or other appropriate handling, subject to
        technical dependencies and applicable requirements.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Confidential information</h2>

      <p>
        Please do not submit passwords, confidential technical
        documents, proprietary datasets, sensitive personal
        information, or other restricted materials through the
        public evaluation-request form.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Privacy inquiries</h2>

      <p>
        You may contact Solo Ghost to inquire about personal
        information associated with your evaluation request,
        including requests for access, correction, or deletion.
        Requests will be reviewed subject to applicable requirements
        and legitimate retention needs.
      </p>

      <p>
        Contact: <a href="mailto:hari.palagiri@gmail.com">hari.palagiri@gmail.com</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>

      <p>
        We may update this policy as our services, operational
        practices, or applicable requirements change.
        The updated version will be published on this page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 24px 96px;
  }

  .privacy-page h1 {
    margin: 16px 0;
  }

  .updated {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .intro {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  section {
    margin-top: 36px;
  }

  section h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  section p,
  section li {
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  section ul {
    padding-left: 24px;
  }
</style>